# Render pipeline

## Ownership

| Concern | Owner |
|---|-----|
| Orchestration, `SupportedFormats`, concurrency gate | `OxyKit.Render.Core/DocumentRenderService` |
| HTTP mapping, 400/500 mapping | `Api/Endpoints/RenderEndpoints.ExecuteRender` |
| Request DTOs | `OxyKit.Render.Contracts/RenderRequests.cs` |
| Sheet/CSV validation & cell typing | `Core/Inputs/TableWorkbookConstraints`, `CsvTableParser`, `IsoDateCell` |
| Emitters | `Core/Outputs/*Renderer` -> `RenderResult` |
| OpenAPI request schemas | `Api/OpenApi/RenderRequestSchemaTransformers.cs` |
| DI registration | `Core/ServiceCollectionExtensions.AddRenderCore` |

## Patterns

- New emitters: `internal sealed`, `RenderAsync(...)`, return `RenderResult(bytes, contentType, fileName)`.
- Bad input -> `ArgumentException` / `NotSupportedException` (becomes 400). Do not invent new error DTO shapes (`ErrorResponse` in Contracts).
- PDF page options via OxyKit.Render `PdfPageSize` / `PdfPageOrientation` and `PdfPageOptionsResolver` (maps to PeachPDF only at emit).
- Template HTML must run through `PrintBaselineInjector.Apply` before return or PDF.
- Put parse/validate/template work inside `DocumentRenderService.ExecuteAsync` so the concurrency gate covers CPU prep.

## Anti-patterns

- Duplicating sheet limits outside `TableWorkbookConstraints`
- Re-enabling PeachPDF HTTP or `file:` loading
- Putting PeachPDF types on request DTOs
- Putting Cloud tenancy/storage into this engine repo
- Referencing `OxyKit.Render.Core` from Cloud (Cloud must use `OxyKit.Render.Client` -> OxyKit.Render API)
